prayerTemplate:
PRAYER

In the light of the facts and circumstances stated above, the Plaintiff most respectfully prays that this Hon'ble Court may graciously be pleased to:

a) Pass a decree of permanent prohibitory injunction under Section 38 of the Specific Relief Act, 1963 restraining the Defendant, his agents, servants, representatives, and persons claiming through or under him, from interfering with the Plaintiff's lawful possession of the suit property described in the Schedule / from {acts_of_defendant};

b) Pass a decree of permanent mandatory injunction under Section 39 of the Specific Relief Act, 1963 directing the Defendant to {mandatory_act} (if applicable);

c) Award costs of the suit in favour of the Plaintiff;

d) Pass any other order(s) as this Hon'ble Court may deem fit and proper.

A separate application under Order 39 Rules 1 and 2 read with Section 151 CPC is being filed seeking temporary injunction pending disposal of the suit.

And for this act of kindness, the Plaintiff shall ever pray.
